-- title:
--   Cross-units separating two nodes, q=3 rigid level
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. The data are: a prime $q$ together with the hypothesis $q = 3$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$; a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. Two function fields occur: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$, and $F =$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, the analogous base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ where $H = \ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times\big)$ is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; the hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le F$ of intermediate fields, and `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` denotes the induced map. For a place $P$ (in the sense of the structure `Place`: a valuation subring containing the base field, proper, with principal ideals), $P.\mathrm{ord}$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ is the value map obtained by inverting `algebraMap` on the residue field (and $0$ off the valuation subring), and $P.\mathrm{IsRational}$ means that `algebraMap` into $P.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective.
--
--   A finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ is given, together with `hW`, which says that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' κ`: the rational, affine geometric places $w$ whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')$ lies in `ssJSet q κ`. A constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is given — a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, with every nonzero element scalable by a constant into the integers with nonzero residue, plus a degree-preserving map on places pushing the divisor of a function to the divisor of its residue — and the hypothesis `hR₀` asserts that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. An element $s \in W$ is fixed, as are $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$.
--
--   On the side of the regular prolongation: a field $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$, a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $F$ to $F_{ss}$ (the same data as a constant reduction, without the map on places), and a finset $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$, with `hcard : N.card = q + 1`. Furthermore, for every place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ there are given a subring $Sx\,Q$ of $F$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_Q : A[X] \to Sx\,Q$, a homomorphism $\chi_{0,Q} : Sx\,Q \to \kappa$ and a set $Dx\,Q$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The hypotheses on this package are: `h0`, that some element of $F_{ss}$ is transcendental over $\kappa$; `h1`, that for every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which satisfies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of the $q$-expansion $j_q$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue the image under `algebraMap κ FSS` of the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue; `h2`, that for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a $q$-th primitive root of unity) and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullback of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is $R.\mathrm{integers}$; `hpkg` (thirteen clauses, summarised here), which requires for each $Q \notin N$ that $Sx\,Q$ contain the constants from $A$, that $\varphi_Q$ be formally smooth and formally unramified and restrict to the identity on constants both in $F$ and after applying $\chi_{0,Q}$, that $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q X) = 0$, that every $c \in A$ with zero residue be the value at $\varphi_Q X$ of a unique section $\chi : Sx\,Q \to A$ lifting $\chi_{0,Q}$ and fixing constants, that every element of $Sx\,Q$ lie in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$ reducing to $\chi_{0,Q}$ of it, that the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q X$ have $Q$-order $1$, that $Dx\,Q$ consist exactly of the rational places $P$ at which all elements of $Sx\,Q$ are regular with values in $A$ and for which $A$-valuation of the value is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_{0,Q}$ kills the element, that sections $\chi$ as above correspond bijectively to points of $Dx\,Q$ via $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$, that membership in the valuation subring of $P \in Dx\,Q$ be equivalent to being a quotient of elements of $Sx\,Q$ with nonvanishing denominator, that a nonzero $f$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f = 0$ for all $P \in Dx\,Q$ become a unit of $Sx\,Q$ after multiplication by a nonzero constant, and that an element of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ regular at all $P \in Dx\,Q$ lie in $Sx\,Q$; `hdisj`, that the discs of distinct places off $N$ are disjoint; `hcusp`, that for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in Dx\,Q$ the image of $j_q$ in $F$ has non-negative $P$-order; and `heqv`, that for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` ($\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced residue automorphism `R.resAut τ hτ` preserves $N$ setwise and, for $Q \notin N$, carries $Dx\,Q$ to $Dx$ of the translated place in the sense of `smulDisc`.
--
--   On the side of the nodes: for every place $x$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ there are a field $FIx\,x$ over $\kappa$, a regular prolongation $Rx\,x$ of $A$ from $F$ to $FIx\,x$ and a place $bx\,x$ of $FIx\,x$ over $\kappa$. Further data: an index type $\Lambda$, subrings $C'\,l \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ contained in $A$ (`hC'A`), each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, elements $\varpi'\,l \in C'\,l$, a distinguished $l_0 \in \Lambda$; rings $Wc\,l$, domains, discrete valuation rings, complete for the adic topology of their maximal ideal, elements $\pi_W\,l$, exponents $E : \Lambda \to \mathbb N$ and $E_0 \in \mathbb N$; sets $S\,nd$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, subrings $\mathcal N\,nd$ and $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ of $F$ with $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ local (`hloc`) and Noetherian (`hnoe`), and elements $cx\,nd$, $cy\,nd$, $cu\,nd$ of $F$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hnodes` is the node presentation, a conjunction whose clauses are: that the residue of $d \in C'\,l$ in $\kappa$ vanishes precisely when $\varpi'\,l \mid d$ in $C'\,l$; that $C'\,l_0 \le C'\,l$ for all $l$; that $\varpi'\,l_0 \ne 0$; that every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'\,l_0$; that each $\pi_W\,l$ is irreducible and $1 \le E\,l$; that every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with `A.tameCharacter π τ = 1` fixes $\varpi'\,l_0$; that $(\varpi'\,l_0)^{E_0} = v\,\pi^{w}$ in $A$ for some unit $v$ of $A$ and some $w \ge 1$; and then, for each $nd \in N$ (a long conjunction, summarised here): rationality of $bx\,nd$, of $nd$ and of all $P \in S\,nd$; the description of $\mathcal N\,nd$ as the elements lying in $(Rx\,nd).\mathrm{integers}$, in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation subring of every $P \in S\,nd$, with $A$-integral values at those $P$; the crossing relation $cx\,nd \cdot cy\,nd = (\varpi'\,l_0)^{E_0}\, cu\,nd$; the branch conditions that the $Rx\,nd$-residue of $cx\,nd$ vanish, that the $R$-residue of $cx\,nd$ have $nd$-order $1$, that the $R$-residue of $cy\,nd$ vanish and that the $Rx\,nd$-residue of $cy\,nd$ have $bx\,nd$-order $1$; invariance of $S\,nd$, $cx\,nd$ and $cy\,nd$ under the semilinear automorphism [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) for $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup with trivial tame character; generation of $F$ as a ring of fractions of the $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ and, with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficients, of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l_0$; and, for each $l$, the chain $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l_0 \le \mathcal N_0\,nd\,l \le \mathcal N\,nd$, the characterisation of $S\,nd$ by regularity of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ and by nonunits having values in the maximal ideal of $A$, the inclusion of the constants $C'\,l$, the approximation of elements of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ by constants modulo nonunits, a $C'\,l$-linear independence property, membership of $cx\,nd$ and $cy\,nd$ in $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ with $cu\,nd$ a unit there, and the existence of a homomorphism $\sigma$ from $Wc\,l$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ and of a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from that completion to the crossing model `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (πW l ^ E l)`, that is $Wc\,l[[U,V]]/(UV - (\pi_W l)^{E\,l})$, matching $\sigma(\pi_W l)$ with $\varpi'\,l$, $\iota \circ \sigma$ with the constants, hitting all constants from $C'\,l$, and converting orders into layers: an element with nonzero $Rx\,nd$-residue of $bx\,nd$-order $n$ is, modulo the ideal generated by $\pi_W l$ and $U$, a unit times $V^n$, and an element with nonzero $R$-residue of $nd$-order $n$ is, modulo the ideal generated by $\pi_W l$ and $V$, a unit times $U^n$. The remaining clauses of `hnodes` assert: the sets $S\,nd$ for distinct $nd \in N$ are disjoint; for $nd \in N$ and $P \in S\,nd$, every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ satisfying the $j_q$-regularity condition with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$ has $P$-value congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to any $a \in A$ whose residue is the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue; for each $\zeta'$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a self-map $\tau N$ of the places of $F_{ss}$ preserving $N$ and matching the translates of the sets $S\,nd$ and the pullbacks of the $(Rx\,nd).\mathrm{integers}$; for $\tau$ in the group generated by the level automorphisms preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, `R.resAut τ hτ` preserves $N$ and carries $S\,nd$ to $S$ of the translated place; for $nd \in N$ the image in $F$ of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $(Rx\,nd).\mathrm{integers}$; and for $nd \in N$ there is a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to $FIx\,nd$ compatible with the residues of $R_0$ and $Rx\,nd$ and with the valuation subrings of $s$ and $bx\,nd$.
--
--   The final hypothesis `hSEP2` is the separation input: for all $x, x' \in N$ with $x \ne x'$ there exist $g \in F$ lying in $\mathcal N_0\,x\,l_0$ and in $\mathcal N_0\,x'\,l_0$, with $cx\,x \in \mathcal N_0\,x\,l_0$, such that $g = cx\,x \cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal N_0\,x\,l_0$, and such that $g$ is a unit of $\mathcal N_0\,x'\,l_0$.
--
--   The conclusion is that for all $x, x' \in N$ with $x \ne x'$ there exists $g \in F$ lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ such that: its $R$-residue is nonzero; the order of that residue at $x$ is nonzero (no value is asserted, only non-vanishing); $P.\mathrm{ord}\,g = 0$ for every $P \in S\,x$; and for every $P \in S\,x'$, $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and its value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,g$, an element of $A$, is a unit of $A$.
--
--   This provides the cross-units used to separate the $q+1$ nodes on the supersingular fibre of the full-level model: for each ordered pair of distinct nodes a function whose reduction has nonzero order at the first node, unit order along the first node's tube, and unit value on the second node's tube. It is the case $q = 3$, carried out under the rigidifying hypothesis of an auxiliary prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, and feeds the assembly statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_exists_nodeAnnuli_nodePresentations_cover_crossUnits_zeroFree_of_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_exists_nodeAnnuli_nodePresentations_cover_crossUnits_zeroFree_of_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
